# `wrangler dev` reads secrets from .dev.vars. That file holds a REAL Cloudflare account token, and the
# repo root's .gitignore covers .env but not this name — so the ignore lives here, next to the thing it
# protects, and is committed before anyone is told to create the file it protects (see README.md).
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# wrangler's local state / build cache.
.wrangler/
